       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. The usual maximum single dose is 850 mg to 1,000 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily** (2,000 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
